From 8893063788040944d71ce3f968819ef99cae6e9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:20:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 313/314] gallium/pvr: blending, depth textures, depth-only and
 unbound-sampler draws

- Blending: fragment variants are keyed by target format and blend state;
  pco lowers the blend from data.fs.blend_opts (rt 0 from the gallium
  blend state, logic ops, colour mask), the blend constants it needs go
  into the shared block from set_blend_color, and the ISP pass type
  follows the variant as the reference picks it (discard: punch-through,
  blending or a masked output: translucent, else opaque).
- Depth formats sample as textures (U16, X8U24, ST8U24, F32; depth reads
  (d, 0, 0, 1)).
- A depth-only framebuffer renders into a scratch colour target of its
  size, and an unbound texture unit reads a 1x1 black texture, instead of
  falling back off the 3D path.

gltri GLTRI_BLEND (alpha 0.5 over green) matches zink's pixel exactly.
glmark2-es2 off-screen runs every draw on the 3D path.
